      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li></li>\n<li></li>\n<li>(I) Joseph b. Perahy\u0101 - may he rest in Eden! - known as Yij\u016b, Mevass\u0113r's brother, humbly beg</li>\n<li>my lord's generosity to allow me to devote myself to you and to be included in the assembly of your clients [...]</li>\n<li></li>\n<li>What I request of your benevolence and hope from your graciousness, is that you kindly write</li>\n<li>in detail to your servant [...] the amount of the goods sent [...]</li>\n<li></li>\n<li></li>\n<li></li>\n<li>He wrote that part of it had been lost. I remain anxious and troubled</li>\n<li>by every aspect. For my brother had written that he determined that the capital, which remained in Fustat after</li>\n<li>most had been lost was 22 Egyptian dinar, from which was purchased pepper for us,</li>\n<li>together. Then he said [= wrote] \\\\to me//: \"The total of your half is 64 pounds of pepper and 22</li>\n<li>Ducan rub\u0101\u02bfis.\" But my agent says: \"Only 65 rub\u0101\u02bfis were given me.\" The verse \"What the cutter has left,</li>\n<li>the locust has devoured\" has been fulfilled in me, as they say, \"Poverty follows the poor.\" For Time has shot its arrows at me.</li>\n<li>I have become impoverished and fate has struck me down. [...]</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
